---
source: system/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help_output(\"fallocate\")"
---
Preallocate or deallocate space to a file

Usage: fallocate [options] <filename>

Arguments:
  <FILENAME>  The file to operate on

Options:
  -l, --length <length>  Length of the range in bytes (required unless --dig-holes)
  -o, --offset <offset>  Offset of the range in bytes [default: 0]
  -n, --keep-size        Do not modify the apparent length of the file
  -c, --collapse-range   Remove a byte range from the file without leaving a hole
  -d, --dig-holes        Detect zeroes and replace with holes
  -i, --insert-range     Insert a hole at the specified offset, shifting existing data
  -p, --punch-hole       Deallocate space (punch a hole) in the byte range
  -z, --zero-range       Zero a byte range in the file
  -x, --posix            Use posix_fallocate(3) compatible operation
  -v, --verbose          Verbose mode
  -h, --help             Print help
